From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mapResampleBuffers_internal: support every accepted
 active-voice cap

setMaxActiveVoiceCount accepts up to VOICE_COUNT - 1, but this function
kept a char live[256] guarded by SOLOUD_ASSERT(mMaxActiveVoices < 256).
On MSVC the assert is a __debugbreak even in release builds (GoreGrind
had to cap at 255); with asserts disabled the memset overran the stack
array. Size it by VOICE_COUNT.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index 26891cf..ef9ced2 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -1929,8 +1929,8 @@ namespace SoLoud
 	{
 		if (!mResampleDataOwner)
 			return; // not initialized; nothing can be mixed yet
-		SOLOUD_ASSERT(mMaxActiveVoices < 256);
-		char live[256];
+		SOLOUD_ASSERT(mMaxActiveVoices < VOICE_COUNT);
+		char live[VOICE_COUNT];
 		memset(live, 0, mMaxActiveVoices);
 		unsigned int i, j;
 		for (i = 0; i < mMaxActiveVoices; i++)
